---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Teleport Bread"
  description="Teleport Bread collects no user data. No accounts, no tracking in the app."
>
  <main>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective September 13, 2026</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Teleport Bread collects <strong>no user data</strong>. The app has no
      accounts, analytics, or tracking. Your reminders stay with Apple.
    </p>

    <h2>How the app works</h2>
    <p>
      Teleport Bread is a user interface layer over Apple Reminders. Your needs,
      notes, and due dates are stored by Apple's Reminders service (EventKit) on
      your device and in your iCloud account, under
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy terms</a>.
      The app reads and writes that data locally, only after you grant Reminders
      access, and sends it nowhere else. We never see it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No data collection, telemetry, or analytics inside the app</li>
      <li>No advertising or analytics SDKs inside the app</li>
      <li>No accounts, sign-ups, or profiles</li>
      <li>No selling or sharing of data — we have nothing to sell or share</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Version and update checks</h2>
    <p>
      At launch, the app fetches a small version file from teleportbread.com to
      learn whether an update is required. No identifiers or reminder data are
      sent. The direct-download Mac app also asks for updates through Sparkle
      once at launch unless you turn automatic checks off in Settings.
    </p>

    <h2>TestFlight betas</h2>
    <p>
      If you join a beta through TestFlight, Apple may share crash logs and
      feedback you choose to submit with us, as described in
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/testflight/">Apple's TestFlight terms</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website (not the app) uses PostHog for anonymous usage analytics —
      page views and similar aggregate statistics — to understand interest in
      the project. No advertising, no cross-site tracking, no sale of data.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href="mailto:help@evbuilds.net">help@evbuilds.net</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding-top: 8vh;
    width: 100%;
  }
  h1 {
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 32px;
    font-size: 20px;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
